                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                        "entry_id": "6d9c3d93-3ced-320d-b536-ea8e0b01a411",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To determine beforehand; predetermine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6dfe68dd-1e9a-4bb7-a3a2-3794a07d88d3",
                                "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                                "text": "The relations of life act as bribes to bias his judgment and foredetermine his verdict."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8de9eec0-50ed-4789-bc68-70a666fdaa0d",
                                "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                                "text": "The answer made to this is, in effect, that although the will is in such a sense a power of contrary choice or self- determination that God cannot foredetermine its action without restraint upon this power and destruction of its freedom [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "928981b8-9a8d-4916-83b5-cf6856132cc1",
                                "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                                "text": "This is not to say that one has access to an eternal blueprint or that one is merely going along with some foredetermined cosmic plan."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8958c604-1788-47e6-9701-7b6da46e8a37",
                                "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                                "text": "But more to the point was Peirce's observation that Carus's reconciliation of religion and science constituted \"an endeavor to reach a foredetermined conclusion.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2987c324-0730-46e2-bb18-2168fd011339",
                                "sense_id": "75bb157d-a1be-3d20-b15e-d4f84c00aa10",
                                "text": "If God plans, foredetermines and predestinates each and every deed of a man's life, powerfully controlling all circumstances, all persons, even all forces of whatever variety and magnitude that affects his life, can that man be truly free?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
